From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep framebuffer swaps out of modem overlay history

Retain only bounded GUI milestones alongside the modem log. Do not capture
the per-swap VEUX GUI trace, which can evict modem/GLINK progress lines.

--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
@@ -1576,6 +1576,11 @@ veux_fb_is_modem_log_line(const char *line)
 		"VEUX MODEM", "VEUX GLINK", "VEUX QRTR", "VEUX WLFW",
 		"VEUX PDMAP", "VEUX IPCC: pa=", "VEUX IPCC: mapped",
-		"VEUX UFS: cached modem_a", "VEUX GUI",
+		"VEUX UFS: cached modem_a",
+		"VEUX GUI STATE", "VEUX GUI SUMMARY",
+		"VEUX GUI: AppleCLCD registered",
+		"VEUX GUI: first valid software display present",
+		"VEUX GUI: IOMFB client initialized",
+		"VEUX GUI: IOMFB client ready",
 	};
 	for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(prefixes) / sizeof(prefixes[0]); ++i) {
 		if (strncmp(line, prefixes[i], strlen(prefixes[i])) == 0) return true;
-- 
